# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values.
# Never commit .env.local or any file containing real secrets.

# Public site URL — used for SEO metadata, sitemap, and robots.txt.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Supabase (database, auth, storage) — create a project at https://supabase.com
# before filling these in. The anon key is safe for the browser; the service
# role key is server-only and must never be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Admin area (docs/ADMIN_ARCHITECTURE.md) — a real, minimal server-side gate
# for /admin, checked in middleware.ts. Both are server-only and must never
# be NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed. Without both set, /admin is blocked entirely
# (fails closed) rather than left open.
# ADMIN_PASSPHRASE: the shared passphrase an admin types in at /admin/login.
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET: a long random string used to sign the session
# cookie — generate one with `openssl rand -base64 32`, for example.
ADMIN_PASSPHRASE=
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# Future payment provider (docs/PAYMENT_ARCHITECTURE.md) — no provider is
# connected today; leaving these unset is correct and keeps
# isPaymentProviderConfigured() (src/lib/payments/is-configured.ts) false,
# which is what keeps every future payment code path failing closed.
# Deliberately generic names, not a specific provider's own variable names
# (never STRIPE_SECRET_KEY or similar) — whichever real provider is chosen
# later fills these in without renaming anything. Both are server-only and
# must never be NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER_ID: the chosen provider's own identifier, once one exists.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER_SECRET_KEY: that provider's server-only secret key.
PAYMENT_PROVIDER_ID=
PAYMENT_PROVIDER_SECRET_KEY=
